    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2024, Australia reaffirmed its strong commitment to public health collaboration by donating 65,000 bottles of antiretroviral medication to Vietnam during a critical national shortage. Delivered in partnership with the World Health Organization (WHO), this timely support ensured uninterrupted treatment for over 178,000 people living with HIV. The Ministry of Health of Vietnam welcomed the donation as a valuable contribution to the country&#x2019;s long-term HIV/AIDS response strategy. This initiative reflects Australia&#x2019;s broader efforts to strengthen Vietnam&#x2019;s capacity to manage communicable disease threats and maintain access to essential healthcare services</narrative>
    </description>
